.TH MGB "1" "August 2026" "mathicgb"
.SH NAME
mgb \- compute Groebner bases and signature Groebner bases
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mgb
.I action
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ project .\|.\|.]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mgb
is the command line interface to mathicgb, a library for computing Groebner
bases and signature Groebner bases using the fast data structures from
mathic.
.PP
Most actions take one or more
.IR project s.
A project is a file name with its extension removed:
.B mgb gb cyclic4
reads
.I cyclic4.ideal
and, if asked to write its result, produces
.IR cyclic4.gb .
.SH ACTIONS
.TP
.B gb
Compute a Groebner basis.
.TP
.B siggb
Compute a signature Groebner basis.
.TP
.B matrix
Perform matrix computations.
.TP
.B help
Return information about the command line interface.
.TP
.B version
Print the mathicgb version.
.SH OPTIONS
Options are specific to each action and are not listed here, as they change
more often than this page does.  Run
.B mgb help
for the list of actions and
.BI "mgb help " action
for the options that action accepts, along with their defaults.
.SH FILES
.TP
.IB project .ideal
Input for
.B gb
and
.BR siggb .
The characteristic of the coefficient field is given first, then the number
of variables, then the monomial order: the number of gradings, a row of
weights for each grading, and optionally order and component keywords such as
.B _revlex
and
.BR revcomponent .
The number of polynomials and the polynomials themselves follow.  All of this
is whitespace separated.  See the
.I examples
directory of the distribution for complete files.
.TP
.IB project .gb
The computed basis, written when the
.B \-outputResult
option is given.
.TP
.IB project .syz
The signatures of the syzygies, written by
.B siggb
when the
.B \-outputResult
option is given.
.TP
.IB project .qmat
A quadruple matrix, read by the
.B matrix
action, which writes the reduced lower right submatrix to
.IB project .brmat
and its reduced form to
.IB project .rbrmat \fR.
.SH EXAMPLES
Compute a Groebner basis of the ideal in
.I cyclic4.ideal
and write it to
.IR cyclic4.gb :
.PP
.RS
.B mgb gb cyclic4 \-outputResult
.RE
.PP
List the options that the
.B gb
action accepts:
.PP
.RS
.B mgb help gb
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
The algorithms are described in "Practical Grobner Basis Computation" by
Bjarke Hammersholt Roune and Michael Stillman, presented at ISSAC 2012 and
available at
.UR http://arxiv.org/abs/1206.6940
.UE .
